      "name": "staging-deploy-watch",
      "prompt": "A deploy pipeline just failed on the project repo. The script above detected this is a NEW failure (not in state tracking). Apply dedup: (1) if there are open kanban fix cards on this branch \u2192 silent exit (fix in flight), (2) if there's an open PR on this branch \u2192 re-trigger CI, (3) neither \u2192 analyze the failure and create a [DF-<timestamp>] fix card on the kanban board with workspace_kind=worktree (never use [GH-] prefix).\n\nBRANCH NAMING: When creating fix cards, the branch name must be unique per task. Append the task ID to the branch name if one is available: fix/df-<timestamp>-<short-name>-<task-id>. This prevents git worktree collisions when two cards target the same branch.",
