    {
      "id": "deea65353907",
      "name": "pr-check-watch",
      "prompt": "Check open PRs on ${HERMES_PROJECT_REPO:-my-org/MyProject} for:\n1. Merge conflicts (where `mergeable` is \"CONFLICTING\" or `mergeStateStatus` is \"DIRTY\")\n2. Failing CI checks (where any status check has failed)\n\nApply the following logic for each open PR (ignoring dependabot PRs where branches start with \"dependabot/\"):\n\n## Case A: Merge Conflicts\nIf a PR has merge conflicts:\n1. **Deduplication**: Check the Kanban board (via SQLite queries or `hermes kanban list`) to see if there is already an active (non-archived, non-done) card on the board containing \"Resolve merge conflicts in <branch>\" in its title or targeting `<branch>`.\n   - SQLite query: `SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE status NOT IN ('done', 'cancelled', 'archived') AND (branch_name = '<branch>' OR title LIKE '%Resolve merge conflicts in <branch>%');`\n   - If an active card exists, skip it.\n2. **Card Creation**: If no active card exists, create a paired coder + reviewer task:\n   - **Coder card**:\n     - Command: `hermes kanban create \"Resolve merge conflicts in <branch>\" --assignee coder --workspace worktree` (Omit `--branch` to let the dispatcher auto-derive a unique worktree branch name to prevent Pattern 5b collisions).\n     - Body:\n       ```\n       ## Goal\n       Resolve Git merge conflicts in pull request branch `<branch>` by merging the latest `main` and resolving conflict markers.\n\n       ## Instructions\n       1. Fetch the original PR branch from origin: `git fetch origin <branch>`\n       2. Merge the PR branch into your current branch: `git merge origin/<branch>`\n       3. Fetch and merge latest main: `git fetch origin main` followed by `git merge origin/main`\n       4. If merge conflicts occur, read the conflicting files, locate the conflict markers, and resolve them by keeping both sides' changes where appropriate or choosing the correct logic.\n       5. Run tests to verify the resolution: `./run-tests.sh` (or appropriate test commands for the changed areas)\n       6. Once tests pass, push your resolved branch directly back to the original PR branch on origin:\n          `git push origin HEAD:<branch>`\n       7. Mark the task complete.\n\n       BASE BRANCH: <branch>\n       CRITICAL: Before writing code, run `git branch --show-current` and verify you are on a worktree branch derived from the base branch above. You must NOT be on main or master. If you are, block the task immediately.\n       ```\n   - **Reviewer card**:\n     - Command: `hermes kanban create \"Review: Resolve merge conflicts in <branch>\" --assignee code-reviewer --parent <coder_task_id>`\n     - Body:\n       ```\n       Review merge conflict resolution for <branch>.\n       Coder task: <coder_task_id>\n       ```\n\n## Case B: Failing CI Checks\nIf a PR has failing CI checks (and does not have merge conflicts):\n1. **Deduplication**: Check the Kanban board to see if there is already an active (non-archived, non-done) card on the board targeting `<branch>`.\n   - SQLite query: `SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE status NOT IN ('done', 'cancelled', 'archived') AND branch_name = '<branch>';`\n   - If an active card exists, skip it.\n2. **Card Creation**: If no active card exists, analyze the failure logs via `gh run view --log-failed` for that PR's latest run, and create a paired coder + reviewer task:\n   - **Coder card**:\n     - Command: `hermes kanban create \"[PRFIX-<timestamp>] Fix failing CI checks on branch <branch>\" --assignee coder --workspace worktree` (Omit `--branch` to avoid Pattern 5b collisions).\n     - Body:\n       ```\n       ## Goal\n       Fix failing CI checks on PR branch `<branch>`.\n\n       ## Failure Details\n       <insert log excerpts and failure analysis here>\n\n       ## Instructions\n       1. Fetch and merge the PR branch into your current branch: `git fetch origin <branch> && git merge origin/<branch>`\n       2. Fix the underlying test or build failure.\n       3. Run the failing tests locally to verify the fix.\n       4. Push the fix directly back to the original PR branch: `git push origin HEAD:<branch>`\n       5. Mark the task complete.\n\n       BASE BRANCH: <branch>\n       CRITICAL: Before writing code, run `git branch --show-current` and verify you are on a worktree branch derived from the base branch above. You must NOT be on main or master. If you are, block the task immediately.\n       ```\n   - **Reviewer card**:\n     - Command: `hermes kanban create \"Review: [PRFIX-<timestamp>] Fix failing CI checks on branch <branch>\" --assignee code-reviewer --parent <coder_task_id>`\n     - Body:\n       ```\n       Review CI fix for <branch>.\n       Coder task: <coder_task_id>\n       ```\n\nUse unique prefix `[PRFIX-<timestamp>]` or `[DF-<timestamp>]` in card titles. Never use the `[GH-N]` prefix in titles as it will trigger automatic issue-closure loops on matching PR numbers.",
