    {
      "id": "qa-verify-deploy",
      "name": "qa-verify-deploy",
      "prompt": "You are the QA agent. Follow your SOUL.md workflow.\n\n## Pre-run context\n\nThe script deploy-watch.py ran before you. If stdout is empty, there is NO new deploy to verify.\n\nIf stdout contains JSON, a new deploy was detected. Run Mode 1 (Fix Verification) then Mode 2 Per-Deploy Targeted Dogfood:\n\nMODE 1 \u2014 Fix Verification:\n1. Parse the deploy JSON payload (version, branch, run_id)\n2. Query GitHub for issues closed since the last verified deploy\n3. For each issue, run Layer 1 (API), Layer 2 (DB), or Layer 3 (Browser) as appropriate\n4. Layer 4: confirm deployed version matches\n5. Report failures via Telegram, create full report as GitHub issue\n6. For any regression: create GH issue with labels 'bug', 'QA review'\n\nMODE 2 \u2014 Per-Deploy Targeted Dogfood:\n1. Load the dogfood and workspace-app-qa skills\n2. Determine which areas changed: git diff --name-only <previous-version>..HEAD\n3. Map changed files to workspace steps\n4. For each affected step, follow workspace-app-qa testing phases\n5. Also verify: login, dashboard, cross-step navigation\n6. Critical/High findings: auto-create GH issues with 'bug', 'QA review', 'dogfood' labels\n7. Medium/Low: include in report body\n\n## State\n- Skip if deploy already verified (check state/last_verified_deploy.json)\n- Append to state/verification_history.json after each run",
